WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.240
At least 27 people are injured and towns are cut off after Panama's magnitude 7.7 quake. This is Omni View Central &amp; South America, episode 18. I'm Mira, the Nerra Network's AI host. It hit Friday at 12.56 Panama time, about 10 kilometers from Patelosa, Ariba in Herrera, and about 196 kilometers from Panama City. O-Globo reports the US Geological Survey first put the quake at 8, then at 7.6, before the figure you just heard.

00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:34.940
Civil protection listed damage to homes, schools, hospitals, churches, government buildings,

00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:36.080
ports and roads.

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:41.580
Renee Garcia, who heads the Emergency Operations Center, told AFP there were no death reports

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.240
at that point.

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:47.620
President Jose Raul Molino said the disaster is large and that roads are totally destroyed.

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:53.080
Health Minister Fernando Boyd said Tono C, in Los Santos, is cut off by land.

00:00:53.460 --> 00:00:58.700
The worst of it is in Los Santos, Herrera, Varagua and Coclei, and authorities have logged

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:04.420
more than 100 aftershocks. Some as strong as magnitude 6. Canal Authority said the waterway,

00:01:04.740 --> 00:01:09.560
about 5% of world sea trade, kept running, while Tokyo man airport shut for a time,

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:14.740
and flights were sent elsewhere. tsunami alerts went out for Costa Rica, Ecuador, Peru,

00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:20.420
Nicaragua, Guatemala, El Salvador, Chile, and Mexico. And Hawaii was flagged too.

00:01:20.920 --> 00:01:24.740
Marco Rubio said the US State Department is moving resources in people to help,

00:01:24.740 --> 00:01:30.640
and the development bank of Latin America gave $250,000 U.S. dollars and opened a $50 million

00:01:30.640 --> 00:01:36.280
emergency line. Across the region, Justice Louise Fuchs has ordered staff at Brazil's Supreme

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:41.340
Court to open his office to confidential inquiries, Justice Alexandra DeMorais is reporting,

00:01:41.880 --> 00:01:47.780
O-Globo reports. Those files involve former President Jair Bolsonaro and allies, including the

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:53.260
Ku-attempt investigation and the fake news inquiry. Columnous Malu Gaspar says a meeting this week

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:56.460
between more eyes and federal police directors set the order off.

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:00.920
The same newsletter ties the moment to a right-wing wave that sent lawmakers to Congress

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:05.460
on a banner of impeaching court ministers, and ministers see two fronts of action after

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:05.900
that wave.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:11.320
In Costa Rica, the state oil company Recope filed preliminary November prices with the

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:14.840
regulator RSEP on Friday, Q. Costa Rica reports.

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:19.280
Regular gasoline would go up 89 colonies to 808 a liter.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:28.020
Super would rise 42 colonies to 806 and diesel 31 colonies to 816. A 25-pound cylinder of

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:34.640
cooking gas, the size most homes use, would climb 547 colonies to 7,719.

00:02:35.320 --> 00:02:39.960
Rekope blames the Middle East crisis, risk on oil shipping routes, and a drop in global

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:45.380
reserves. RSEP still has to review the filing. The new prices hit in the first days of November

00:02:45.380 --> 00:02:47.060
or only if that review approves them.

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:51.300
Also today, Chile has declared Los Condes in eastern Santiago

00:02:51.520 --> 00:02:54.280
a disaster zone after flash floods and mudslides

00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:56.780
with more than 1,000 residents evacuated,

00:02:57.180 --> 00:02:58.080
Al Jazeera reports.

00:02:58.780 --> 00:03:01.540
Franco Colapinto retired early from the Singapore Sprint

00:03:01.540 --> 00:03:04.080
after Alpine lost all data and radio contact

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:05.980
with the car, La Nacion reports.

00:03:06.660 --> 00:03:08.840
Argentina meets the wider world of data centers

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:10.600
with 67 registered sites,

00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.640
52 already running and 13 still announced.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:18.660
the Buenos Aires Times reports. The government is looking at billions of dollars for that buildout.

00:03:19.000 --> 00:03:24.660
The Times also reports growing worry over energy use, water, and how many jobs the sites actually create.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:30.960
The case on both sides in the same O-Globo newsletter is when legal steps around Jair Bolsonaro should move,

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:32.720
with the second round still ahead.

00:03:33.260 --> 00:03:37.600
Justice Nunes Marquez evaluates that a criminal review should wait until after that round,

00:03:37.880 --> 00:03:42.160
because the step could interfere in the elections, and that the request should go to the full court.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.460
That is his assessment.

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:45.400
The plenary has not voted it.

00:03:45.780 --> 00:03:50.700
Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, the PL presidential candidate, has made a pardon for his father

00:03:50.700 --> 00:03:52.460
one of the promises he repeats most.

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:56.540
The newsletter describes the former president as convicted of attempting a coup.

00:03:57.220 --> 00:04:01.060
Jurists in that newsletter ask whether he could grant the pardon in time to take the inaugural

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.180
ramp with his father.

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.940
The case they frame for moving is that repeated promise in that calendar.

00:04:06.480 --> 00:04:11.100
Both treatments take the conviction, as O. Globo states it, as the fact in front of them.

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:13.360
The pardon remains a campaign promise.

00:04:13.820 --> 00:04:18.440
A sign of progress in a finished result or a measured recovery is not in today's reporting.

00:04:19.080 --> 00:04:19.780
The day had none.

